<h2 id="massing">1. Monolithic Stone & Steel Geometries</h2>
<p>Modern residential architecture hinges on the bold equilibrium between mass and void. Strategic cantilevers and monolithic building blocks create dramatic silhouettes against the horizon while framing intimate views of surrounding terrain.</p>

<h2 id="glazing">2. Directional Solar Grazing & Shadow Play</h2>
<p>Expansive high-performance glazing invites dynamic daylight shifts into living volumes while high-performance solar coatings reduce solar heat gain. At dusk, architectural uplighting highlights structural textures.</p>

<h2 id="materials">3. Tactile Exterior Material Layering</h2>
<p>Contrast raw, heavy materials like board-formed concrete or slate with warm cedar slatting and ultra-slim aluminum framing for timeless curb appeal.</p>

<h2 id="shop">4. Shop the Architectural Elements</h2>
<p>Incorporate the clean lines of this modern architectural home with curated exterior sconces, minimalist house numbers, and concrete planters below.</p>
